---
components: ["AILabel", "AILabelActions"]
description: AI labels mark content and fields generated by AI, and open an explanation of how the AI produced them.
---

<script>
  import {
    AILabel,
    AILabelActions,
    Button,
    ComboBox,
    DatePicker,
    DatePickerInput,
    Dropdown,
    NumberInput,
    Select,
    SelectItem,
    Stack,
    TextArea,
    TextInput,
    Checkbox,
    CheckboxGroup,
    RadioButton,
    RadioButtonGroup,
    Tag,
    Tile,
    SelectableTile,
  } from "carbon-components-svelte";
</script>

## Basic

Click the label to open the explanation. Put the explanation in the default slot.

<AILabel>
  <p class="bx--label">AI explained</p>
  <p>This forecast was generated from the last 90 days of usage across your workspace.</p>
</AILabel>

## Sizes

Set `size` to control the button size. The default is `"xs"`.

<Stack orientation="horizontal" gap={5}>
  <AILabel size="mini" />
  <AILabel size="2xs" />
  <AILabel size="xs" />
  <AILabel size="sm" />
  <AILabel size="md" />
  <AILabel size="lg" />
  <AILabel size="xl" />
</Stack>

## Inline

Set `kind` to `"inline"` to render the label as text. Use `textLabel` to add text beside it.

<Stack orientation="horizontal" gap={5}>
  <AILabel kind="inline" size="sm" />
  <AILabel kind="inline" size="md" textLabel="Generated summary" />
  <AILabel kind="inline" size="lg" textLabel="Generated summary" />
</Stack>

## Actions

Add `AILabelActions` at the end of the explanation for related actions. The bar runs along the bottom edge of the explanation, and a primary button sits last.

<AILabel>
  <p class="bx--label">AI explained</p>
  <p>Anomalies were flagged by comparing request latency with the same hour last week.</p>
  <AILabelActions>
    <Button kind="ghost">View details</Button>
    <Button>Tune model</Button>
  </AILabelActions>
</AILabel>

## Fields

Put an AI label in the `decorator` slot of a field to mark its value as AI-generated. The field shows the AI gradient, and the label always renders at the `"mini"` size. Text inputs, text areas, number inputs, selects, dropdowns, combo boxes, multiselects, and date pickers have the slot.

<Stack gap={6} style="max-width: 320px">
  <TextInput labelText="Incident title" value="Database failover in us-east-1">
    <AILabel slot="decorator">
      <p>Suggested from the alert that opened this incident.</p>
    </AILabel>
  </TextInput>
  <TextArea labelText="Summary" value="Primary database failed over after a storage node stopped responding.">
    <AILabel slot="decorator" />
  </TextArea>
  <NumberInput labelText="Replicas" value={3}>
    <AILabel slot="decorator" />
  </NumberInput>
  <Select labelText="Severity" selected="sev2">
    <SelectItem value="sev1" text="Sev 1" />
    <SelectItem value="sev2" text="Sev 2" />
    <AILabel slot="decorator" />
  </Select>
  <Dropdown labelText="Owning team" selectedId="db" items={[{ id: "db", text: "Database platform" }, { id: "net", text: "Networking" }]}>
    <AILabel slot="decorator" />
  </Dropdown>
  <ComboBox labelText="Region" selectedId="us-east-1" items={[{ id: "us-east-1", text: "US East (N. Virginia)" }, { id: "eu-west-1", text: "EU West (Ireland)" }]}>
    <AILabel slot="decorator" />
  </ComboBox>
  <DatePicker datePickerType="single">
    <DatePickerInput labelText="Follow-up date" placeholder="mm/dd/yyyy">
      <AILabel slot="decorator" />
    </DatePickerInput>
  </DatePicker>
</Stack>

## Selection controls

Checkboxes, radio buttons, and their groups have a `decorator` slot too. The label follows the label text or the legend.

<Stack gap={5}>
  <Checkbox labelText="Enable automatic failover" checked>
    <AILabel slot="decorator" />
  </Checkbox>
  <RadioButtonGroup legendText="Billing cycle" selected="annual">
    <AILabel slot="decorator" />
    <RadioButton labelText="Monthly" value="monthly" />
    <RadioButton labelText="Annual" value="annual" />
  </RadioButtonGroup>
</Stack>

## Tags

In a tag, the label renders as inline text in the tag's color.

<Tag type="blue">Forecast<AILabel slot="decorator" /></Tag>
<Tag type="green" filter>us-east-1<AILabel slot="decorator" /></Tag>

## Tiles

Tiles, clickable tiles, selectable tiles, radio tiles, and expandable tiles show the AI surface and put the label in the top-right corner. On interactive tiles, the label sits outside the link, button, or label element.

<Stack orientation="horizontal" gap={5}>
  <Tile style="width: 16rem">
    <h4>Usage forecast</h4>
    <p>Spend is projected to grow 12% next month.</p>
    <AILabel slot="decorator" />
  </Tile>
  <SelectableTile style="width: 16rem">
    Recommended plan: Team
    <AILabel slot="decorator" />
  </SelectableTile>
</Stack>

## Data tables

A data table has three slots: `decorator` beside the title, `headerDecorator` for AI columns, and `rowDecorator` for AI rows. See [DataTable](/components/DataTable#ai-label).

<FileSource src="/framed/DataTable/DataTableAILabel" />

## Modals

`Modal` and `ComposedModal` show the AI surface and put the label beside the close button. See [Modal](/components/Modal#ai-label).

<FileSource src="/framed/Modal/ModalAILabel" />

## Revert

Set `revertActive` to `true` after the user edits an AI-generated value. The label turns into a revert button. Clicking it sets `revertActive` back to `false` and dispatches `revert`, so you can restore the AI value.

<FileSource src="/framed/AILabel/AILabelRevert" />

## Direction and alignment

Set `direction` and `align` to place the explanation. Inside a field, the explanation aligns to the end of the label by default; elsewhere it aligns to the start.

<AILabel direction="right" align="start">
  <p>Generated from your last three billing cycles.</p>
</AILabel>

## Portal

Set `portalTooltip` to `true` to render the explanation in a portal, so a container with `overflow: hidden` cannot clip it. Inside a `Modal`, the explanation is portalled by default.

<div style="overflow: hidden; padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--cds-border-subtle)">
  <AILabel portalTooltip>
    <p>Generated from your last three billing cycles.</p>
  </AILabel>
</div>
